    "parts":  [
                  "Charging your phone all night? It won't overcharge.",
                  "Battery University: a lithium-ion charger turns off the current when it's full.",
                  "The fear comes from older nickel-cadmium batteries and their famous \"memory.\"",
                  "Lithium-ion has no memory.",
                  "But there is a catch.",
                  "Sitting at 100 percent for hours can wear a battery more than normal use.",
                  "Worst case: full and hot.",
                  "That's why your iPhone can wait to finish charging until just before you unplug.",
                  "Newer iPhones even let you stop at 80 percent.",
                  "So charge overnight. Just don't let it cook under your pillow."
              ],
